  Gaps:
  Now I have a full picture. Here's the complete gap analysis organized by priority:

  ---
  🔴 Critical — Blockers for Production

  1. No HTTPS
  ALB only has an HTTP:80 listener. No ACM certificate exists in the account. All traffic —
  including auth tokens — is sent in plaintext.
  → Provision ACM cert for chat.deeptechexpertconsulting.com, add HTTPS:443 listener, redirect
  HTTP→HTTPS.

  2. RDS storage not encrypted at rest
  StorageEncrypted: False on chatapp-db01. AWS cannot enable encryption on a running cluster —
  requires snapshot → restore into a new encrypted cluster.

  3. RDS deletion protection off
  DeletionProtection: False. One accidental aws rds delete-db-cluster drops the production
  database permanently.
  → One CLI call: aws rds modify-db-cluster --deletion-protection.

  4. Plaintext secrets in values files
  db.password: password01 is in values-dev.yaml in plaintext. values-prod-secrets.yaml sits on
  disk unencrypted. No AWS Secrets Manager or External Secrets Operator in use.

  5. Aurora MySQL 5.7 — EOL
  Running aurora-mysql 2.11.1 (MySQL 5.7 compatible). MySQL 5.7 reached end-of-life October 2025.
   No security patches. Must upgrade to Aurora MySQL 3.x (MySQL 8.0 compatible).

  ---
  🟠 Security Gaps

  6. No WAF on the ALB
  No WebACL attached. The app is exposed directly to the internet with no rate limiting, SQL
  injection protection, or bot filtering.

  7. No pod security context
  Containers run as root with full privileges. No runAsNonRoot, no readOnlyRootFilesystem, no
  allowPrivilegeEscalation: false.

  8. No Kubernetes NetworkPolicy
  All pods can talk to all other pods across all namespaces. No ingress/egress restrictions
  enforced at the network layer.

  9. No KMS envelope encryption for etcd
  cluster.encryptionConfig: null — Kubernetes Secrets (including chatapp-secret with DATABASE_URL
   and SECRET_KEY) are stored unencrypted in etcd.

  10. No dedicated pod ServiceAccount
  Pods use the default ServiceAccount. Best practice is a dedicated SA with minimal IRSA
  permissions so a compromised pod can't escalate.

  11. ALB deletion protection off
  deletion_protection.enabled: false — the ALB can be deleted accidentally.

  ---
  🟡 Reliability Gaps

  12. RDS single-AZ, single instance
  MultiAZ: False, one instance (db.t3.small) in us-east-1a only. Any AZ failure or instance
  failure = full outage with no automatic failover.
  → Add an Aurora Replica in us-east-1b.

  13. ElastiCache single-AZ
  MultiAZ: disabled despite AutoFailover: enabled. Failover has nowhere to fail over to.
  → Enable Multi-AZ on the replication group.

  14. No Pod Disruption Budget
  With 2 replicas and Karpenter consolidating every 30 seconds, both pods can be evicted
  simultaneously during a node drain.
  → Add PodDisruptionBudget with minAvailable: 1.

  15. ALB idle timeout too short for WebSockets
  idle_timeout: 60s. The app has WebSocket routes. A 60-second idle timeout will silently drop
  long-lived WS connections.
  → Increase to 3600s (matches the nginx annotations that were there originally).

  16. Container image pinned to latest
  morganokanyair/chat-api:latest is not reproducible — a bad push can silently roll out a broken
  image. Deployments cannot be reliably rolled back.
  → Pin to a digest or semver tag in CI/CD.

  ---
  🔵 Observability Gaps

  17. ALB access logs disabled
  No HTTP request logs. Cannot audit traffic, debug errors, or detect abuse after the fact.
  → Enable to an S3 bucket with lifecycle policy.

  18. No centralized log aggregation
  Pod logs exist only in kubelet memory. Node replacement (every 14 days via Karpenter
  expireAfter) destroys them.
  → CloudWatch Container Insights, Fluent Bit, or similar.

  19. No alerting
  Prometheus metrics are exposed and scraped but there is no Alertmanager and no CloudWatch
  alarms — nobody gets paged on pod crashes, OOM, or latency spikes.

  ---
  ⚪ Operational / Hygiene

  20. No CI/CD pipeline
  Deployments are manual Helm CLI invocations from a local machine. No reproducible, auditable
  deploy process.

  21. ElastiCache cache.t4g.micro undersized
  Fine for dev, not for production traffic. Needs capacity planning.

  22. No container image vulnerability scanning
  No ECR image scan or Trivy in the pipeline — known CVEs in base image ship to prod undetected.

